# Requirements checklist (global hard rule)

## Canonical contract file (per project)

```
.cursor/REQUIREMENTS.md
```

- This is the acceptance contract for the current task set.
- `SESSION_HANDOFF.md` is context/summary only — not the requirements list.
- Create `.cursor/` if missing. Do not put secrets in this file.

## Ownership flow

1. `requirements-manager` gathers atomic requirements (or Tiny inline extract).
2. Implementation agent works the checklist.
3. `acceptance-review` verifies against the checklist and repo.

## Hidden work (policy C)

- Broad scope only (e.g. “premium”, “whole app”, “entire page look”): expand implied UX/quality items into **must-pass** checklist rows.
- Narrow scope: do **not** expand; keep implied items as notes / nice-to-haves.
- Always **notify the user what was discarded** (not expanded into must-pass).

## Do not

- Reduce scope when writing requirements (e.g. “whole app” → “login only”).
- Merge unrelated requests into one row.
- Mark incomplete work complete.
